  <content>
  <section><emphasis><emphasis>
  <para>Students will complete the following questions to practice the skills they have learned in this lesson.</para>
</emphasis></emphasis>
<para>Use the following scenario to answer questions 1 – 5.</para>
<blockquote>
<para>Based on past musical productions, a theater predicts selling \(400-8p\) tickets when each ticket is sold at \(p\) dollars.</para>
</blockquote>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
<item>Answer questions a–g to complete the middle column in the table to find out how many tickets the theater expects to sell and what revenues it expects to receive at the given ticket prices.</item>
</list>
<table class="os-raise-wideequaltable">
<thead>
  <row>
    <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">Ticket price (dollars)</entry>
    <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">Number of tickets sold</entry>
    <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">Revenue (dollars)</entry>
  </row>
</thead>
<tbody>
  <row>
    <entry>
      <para><emphasis>Ticket price (dollars)</emphasis></para>
    </entry>
    <entry>
      <para><emphasis>Number of tickets sold</emphasis></para>
    </entry>
    <entry>
      <para><emphasis>Revenue (dollars)</emphasis></para>
    </entry>
  </row>
  <row>
    <entry>
      <para>\(5\)</para>
    </entry>
    <entry>
      <para>\(360\)</para>
    </entry>
    <entry>
      <para>\(1800\)</para>
    </entry>
  </row>
  <row>
    <entry>
      <para>\(10\)</para>
    </entry>
    <entry>
      <para>a. _____</para>
    </entry>
    <entry> </entry>
  </row>
  <row>
    <entry>
      <para>\(15\)</para>
    </entry>
    <entry>
      <para>b. _____</para>
    </entry>
    <entry> </entry>
  </row>
  <row>
    <entry>
      <para>\(20\)</para>
    </entry>
    <entry>
      <para>c. _____</para>
    </entry>
    <entry> </entry>
  </row>
  <row>
    <entry>
      <para>\(30\)</para>
    </entry>
    <entry>
      <para>d. _____</para>
    </entry>
    <entry> </entry>
  </row>
  <row>
    <entry>
      <para>\(45\)</para>
    </entry>
    <entry>
      <para>e. _____</para>
    </entry>
    <entry> </entry>
  </row>
  <row>
    <entry>
      <para>\(50\)</para>
    </entry>
    <entry>
      <para>f. _____</para>
    </entry>
    <entry> </entry>
  </row>
  <row>
    <entry>
      <para>\(p\)</para>
    </entry>
    <entry>
      <para>g. _____</para>
    </entry>
    <entry> </entry>
  </row>
</tbody>
</table>

<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item> When the price is \($10\) per ticket, what is the number of tickets sold? </item>
  
  <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(320\)</para>
</list>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item> When the price is \($15\) per ticket, what is the number of tickets sold? </item>
  
  <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(280\)</para>
</list>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item> When the price is \($20\) per ticket, what is the number of tickets sold? </item>
  
  <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(240\)</para>
</list>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
  <item> When the price is \($30\) per ticket, what is the number of tickets sold? </item>
  
  <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(160\)</para>
</list>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
  <item> When the price is \($45\) per ticket, what is the number of tickets sold?
    <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(40\)</para>
  </item>
</list>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="6" type="enumerated">
  <item> When the price is \($50\) per ticket, what is the number of tickets sold? </item>
  
  <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(0\)</para>
</list>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="7" type="enumerated">
  <item> When the price is \(p\) per ticket, what is the number of tickets sold? </item>
</list>
</list>
<list>
<item> \(400-8p\) </item>
<item> \(p(400-8p)\) </item>
<item> \(p(8p-400)\) </item>
<item> \(392p\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(400-8p\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
<item>Answer questions a-g to complete the right column in the table to find out what revenues the theater expects to receive at the given ticket prices.</item>
</list>
<table class="os-raise-wideequaltable">
<thead>
  <row>
    <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">Ticket price (dollars)</entry>
    <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">Number of tickets sold</entry>
    <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">Revenue (dollars)</entry>
  </row>
</thead>
<tbody>
  <row>
    <entry>
      <para>\(5\)</para>
    </entry>
    <entry>
      <para>\(360\)</para>
    </entry>
    <entry>
      <para>\(1800\)</para>
    </entry>
  </row>
  <row>
    <entry>
