<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item> When the price is \($10\) per ticket, what is the revenue in dollars? </item>
  
  <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(3,200\)</para>
</list>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item> When the price is \($15\) per ticket, what is the revenue in dollars? </item>
  
  <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(4,200\)</para>
</list>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item> When the price is \($20\) per ticket, what is the revenue in dollars? </item>
  
  <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(4,800\)</para>
</list>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
  <item> When the price is \($30\) per ticket, what is the revenue in dollars? </item>
  
  <para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>\(4,800\)</para>
</list>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
  <item> When the price is \($45\) per ticket, what is the revenue in dollars? </item>
  
  <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(1,800\)</para>
</list>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="6" type="enumerated">
  <item> When the price is \($50\) per ticket, what is the revenue in dollars? </item>
  
  <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(0\)</para>
</list>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="7" type="enumerated">
  <item> When the price is \(p\) per ticket, what is the revenue in dollars?</item>
</list>
</list>
<list>
<list>
  <item> \(p(400-8p)\) </item>
  <item> \(p(8p-400)\) </item>
  <item> \(400-8p\) </item>
  <item> \(392p\) </item>
</list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>\(p(400-8p)\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
<item>For which ticket price, listed in the table, will the theater earn no revenue?</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(50\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
<item>Calculate the lowest price of a ticket that the theater should sell the tickets for if it must earn at least \($3,200\) in revenue to break even (to not lose money) on the musical production. (The calculated value may not be listed in the table.)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(10\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
<item>Calculate the highest price of a ticket that the theater should sell the tickets for if it must earn at least \($3,200\) in revenue to break even (to not lose money) on the musical production. (The calculated value may not be listed in the table.)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(40\). Although not shown in the table, we can calculate that when \(p\) is \($40\), the expected revenue is \(40(400-8(40))\) or \(40 \cdot 80\), which is \($3,200\).</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="6" type="enumerated">
<item>A company sells running shoes. If the price of a pair of shoes in dollars is \(p\), the company estimates that it will sell \(50,000-400p\) pairs of shoes.</item>
</list>
<para>Which expression represents the revenue in dollars from selling running shoes if a pair of shoes is priced at \(p\) dollars?</para>
<list>
<list>
  <item> \((50,000-400p) \cdot p\) </item>
  <item> \((50,000p-400) \cdot p\) </item>
  <item> \((50,000p-400p)\) </item>
  <item> \((49,600p) \cdot p\)</item>
</list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \((50,000-400p) \cdot p\)</para>
<para>Use the following scenario to answer questions 7 – 10.</para>
<blockquote>
The function \(f\) represents the revenue in dollars the school can expect to receive if it sells \(220-12x\) coffee mugs for \(x\) dollars each.
</blockquote>
<para>Here is the graph of \(f\).</para>
<para><figure><media alt="Parabola on grid. Horizontal axis, price in dollars, from 0 to 20. Vertical axis, revenue in dollars, from 0 to 1000. Parabola opens down. Vertex near 9 comma 1000. \(\(x\)-intercepts near 0 and 18 point 2."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/705dd39386a32f3133aec603e335440f11bbffdb"/></media></figure></para>

<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="7" type="enumerated">
<item>Select <emphasis>three</emphasis> statements that describe this situation.</item>
</list>
<list>
<item> At \($2\) per coffee mug, the revenue will be \($196\). </item>
<item> The school expects to sell \(160\) mugs if the price is \($5\) each. </item>
<item> The school will lose money if it sells the mugs for more than \($10\) each. </item>
<item> The school will earn about \($1,000\) if it sells the mugs for \($10\) each. </item>
<item> The revenue will be more than \($700\) if the price is between \($5\) and \($14\). </item>
<item> The expected revenue will increase if the price per mug is greater than \($10\). </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> The school expects to sell \(160\) mugs if the price is \($5\) each. The school will earn about \($1,000\) if it sells the mugs for \($10\) each. The revenue will be more than \($700\) if the price is between \($5\) and \($14\).</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="8" type="enumerated">
<item>To the nearest hundred dollars, what is the maximum revenue for the mugs?</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>\(1,000\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="9" type="enumerated">
<item>Which is the approximate domain?</item>
</list>
<list>
<item> \(0 \leq x \leq 18\) </item>
<item> \(0 \leq x \leq 9\) </item>
<item> \(0 \leq x \leq 1000\) </item>
<item> \(x \geq 0\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>\(0 \leq x \leq 18\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="10" type="enumerated">
<item>Which is the approximate range? </item>
</list>
<list>
<item>\(0  \leq y  \lt \infty\)</item>
  <item>\(0 \leq y  \leq 1000\)</item>
  <item>\(y  \leq 1000\)</item>
  <item>\(-\infty \lt y  \leq 1000\)</item>

</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(0  \leq y  \leq 1000\)</para>
<para> </para>
</section>
